      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nothing changed, and I remember the previous conclusion is making `isNetworkSupported` and `setNetworkSupported` as hidden API. Current setting is just for the initial draft to write a code with testing.\n\nBut to do so, we cannot use those APIs for constructing a test in `MicrodroidTests` without `@TestApi`.\nAnd I believe we would need to expose this as `@SystemApi` to use Java API in `VmLauncherApp`, which is running ferrochrome on top of our Java API nowadays.\n\nI also had a doubt about API expose and flagging while writing draft code, so I want to check again which one is proper. But, hidden API(neither `@SystemApi` nor `@TestApi`) is not a good choice, since we lose the chance to test.",
